## Source
2026-06-04 foundations audit (Communicate). Live contracts stated only
in the French charter or CHANGELOG -- places a contributor does not
read before editing the code:
- "install est le seul verbe qui mute hors de tickets/" --
  erg-imagine-charter.md:42 + CHANGELOG.md:22 only.
- migrate's asset refresh is DELIBERATELY force-overwrite, exempt from
  the dpkg prompt -- erg-imagine-charter.md:124-127 only (and the
  outcome of 0224 may amend the behavior for .ergrc).
Also: the seven invariants have no compact user-facing statement;
README sells hand-edit-wins and offline but never lists them.

## Fix
1. AGENTS.md (or erg-manual.md where it fits better): state
   install-is-the-only-outside-mutating-verb as a rule with its why.
2. Document migrate's asset-refresh policy in erg-manual.md
   consistently with whatever 0224 lands (deliberate force-overwrite,
   carve-out, or 3-state).
3. README: a seven-bullet invariants block -- one line each, linking
   AGENTS.md for the law and the PEP for the why. Repetition is
   deliberate here and stops at one copy.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] install-only-outside-mutator stated outside the charter
- [ ] migrate asset-refresh policy documented, matching 0224 outcome
- [ ] README invariants block present, pointing at AGENTS.md + PEP
- [ ] make check passes

## Imagine (raid 2026-06-04)
- Why now: Two live contributor contracts -- install-is-the-only-outside-mutating-verb and migrate's asset-refresh exemption -- exist only in the French charter (docs/erg-imagine-charter.md:42, 124-127) and CHANGELOG:22. A contributor editing the code never reads those; root /AGENTS.md and the manual are the documents they do read. The gap is real (grep of /AGENTS.md and src/go/assets/AGENTS.md both return zero hits for the install-only rule). The README sells offline and hand-edit-wins but never gives users the compact seven-invariant view already present in /AGENTS.md lines 24-54; the link is missing, not the content.
- Scope check: Sub-task 1 (install-only rule) -- genuine gap; lands in root /AGENTS.md (contributor-facing policy), NOT in src/go/assets/AGENTS.md (adopter template) and NOT in erg-manual.md (generated artifact). Sub-task 2 (migrate policy) -- 0224 has landed; docs/erg-manual.md lines 368-370 already state the settled policy verbatim (AGENTS.md force-overwrite, .ergrc excluded, config delivered by erg init). This sub-task reduces to verifying the landed text matches exit-criteria intent -- no new writing required. Sub-task 3 (README block) -- the seven invariants already exist in root /AGENTS.md:24-54; the README needs one block that names them and links there + PEP, not a re-paste.
- Simplest path: (1) Append one paragraph to root /AGENTS.md under the invariants section: install is the only verb that mutates outside tickets/, and only behind explicit opt-in flags, because all other verbs must stay offline and scope-confined. (2) Verify docs/erg-manual.md migrate section matches 0224 intent (already done -- PASS). (3) Add a "Seven operating invariants" bullet block to README after the "Why it's a no-brainer" section: seven one-liners keyed to the names in /AGENTS.md, with links to /AGENTS.md (law) and pep-erg-v1.md (why). Total diff: ~15-20 lines across two files; make check to close. Note: erg-manual.md is 100% generated from erg --help --all (Makefile:140; header "Generated from: erg") -- if migrate helptext ever needs updating, it must route through helptext.go + make docs, never hand-edited; current text needs no change.
- Antipattern scan: Doc-drift risk if the install-only rule is added to src/go/assets/AGENTS.md instead of root /AGENTS.md -- the adopter template would gain a git-erg-internal policy rule that confuses users of erg in their own projects. Route to root /AGENTS.md only. YAGNI: sub-task 2 is already satisfied; do not re-document what the manual already states correctly. Copy-proliferation: README block must link, not re-paste the invariants -- the ticket already says "stops at one copy"; confirm Execute honors this. No other antipattern found.

## Plan (raid 2026-06-04)

### Actions

1. AGENTS.md (root, line 55 -- after the Small bullet, before the blank line at 55):
   Append one paragraph after the seven-invariants list (after line 54 "...0146 guards it)."):

   "Scope confinement: `install` is the only verb that mutates outside `tickets/` (`.git/hooks`
   and the root `AGENTS.md` pointer), and only behind explicit opt-in flags (`--hooks`,
   `--inject-agents`) that default to off. Every other verb stays confined to `tickets/` and
   offline. This is the implementation of the Offline and Agnostic invariants at the command
   boundary -- a contributor adding a new verb must respect the same scope."

   Insertion: after line 54 of AGENTS.md (the closing parenthesis of the Small bullet),
   before the blank line that precedes "Audits are the evidence engine." (current line 56).
   This places the rule inside the invariants section, immediately after the enumeration.

   CONFIRMED: root /AGENTS.md is hand-maintained. It is NOT generated, NOT embedded in
   src/go/assets/, and NOT covered by the selfcoherence byte-comparison guard. The
   selfcoherence guard (tests/test_selfcoherence.sh lines 44-56) compares
   tickets/AGENTS.md against src/go/assets/AGENTS.md -- root /AGENTS.md is a completely
   separate file. No guard constrains what may be added to root /AGENTS.md.

2. docs/erg-manual.md -- no action required.
   VERIFIED: lines 367-374 already state the settled 0224 policy verbatim:
   "tickets/AGENTS.md (force-overwrite, no prompt -- agent docs track the binary;
   .ergrc is configuration, delivered by 'erg init', so run 'erg update && erg init'
   to refresh it with the dpkg 3-state rule that preserves local edits)".
   This matches exit-criterion intent exactly. Sub-task 2 is DONE.

3. README.md -- insert a "Seven operating invariants" block after the "Why it's a
   no-brainer" section (after line 51 -- the Agent-native bullet -- before the blank
   line and "## Want more?" heading at line 53).

   Draft block (7 lines, one per invariant, linking AGENTS.md law + PEP why):

   "## Seven operating invariants

   The `erg` CLI is built on seven non-negotiable properties (law: [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md),
   rationale: [pep-erg-v1.md](pep-erg-v1.md)):

   - **Never lose data** -- atomic write, validate-before-replace, no truncation on kill.
   - **Agnostic** -- hand edit always wins; the plain `.erg` file is the contract.
   - **Offline** -- zero network calls; listing work is a local file read.
   - **Standalone** -- one static binary plus POSIX; zero third-party dependencies.
   - **Stateless** -- files are the only state; no pending/claimed/doing tags.
   - **Fast** -- linear in corpus size; invoked per-commit, per-push, in agent loops.
   - **Small** -- binary committed and travels with every clone; size is paid by all."

   Insertion: after README.md line 51 (end of the "Why it's a no-brainer" bullet list),
   before the blank line leading into "## Want more? Add the erg binary (optional)".
   This creates EXACTLY ONE copy of the invariant names in README -- the block names
   them and links to AGENTS.md (where the full authoritative text lives) and pep-erg-v1.md
   (where the rationale lives). It does NOT re-paste the law text.

   CONFIRMED: no test in test_docs.sh constrains the README heading count or section
   order in the area of the insertion. The existing tests check: (a) no bare-ID erg validate
   example, (b) install step names tickets/erg, (c) CONTRIBUTING.md checklist tokens.
   None of these are affected by adding a new section between lines 51-53.

   CONFIRMED: test_encoding.sh ASCII guard covers src/go/** only -- it does NOT scan
   README.md or root AGENTS.md. Both target files are free of encoding constraints.

### First test

Run `make check` (= make test + make validate) after applying both edits.
The affected suites are:
- tests/test_docs.sh -- verifies the README is consistent (existing checks unaffected;
  the new block introduces no bare IDs and does not touch the install step wording).
- tests/test_selfcoherence.sh -- not affected (root /AGENTS.md is not in scope).
- tests/test_encoding.sh -- not affected (neither README nor root AGENTS.md is scanned).
- make validate (erg check tickets/) -- must pass on the ticket file itself.

Manual spot-check: grep for "Seven operating invariants" in README.md and for
"Scope confinement" in AGENTS.md to confirm insertion landed correctly.

### Dependencies

- 0224 (migrate asset-refresh policy) -- already merged. Sub-task 2 verified DONE.
- No other open blockers.

### Drift scan

- Root /AGENTS.md is hand-maintained, separate from src/go/assets/AGENTS.md (the adopter
  template). Adding the install-only paragraph to root /AGENTS.md creates no copy in the
  adopter template and does not trigger the selfcoherence guard. Safe.
- README block names the seven invariants by their canonical names and links to AGENTS.md.
  The law text itself remains in AGENTS.md only -- no copy proliferation.
- docs/erg-manual.md is 100% generated (make docs from erg --help --all); it is not
  touched by this ticket. The migrate policy already in it (lines 367-374) is the
  authoritative post-0224 statement; no parallel copy is introduced.
- src/go/assets/AGENTS.md (adopter template) is NOT modified -- adding git-erg-internal
  contributor policy there would confuse adopters. Confirmed no drift risk.
